{"kind":"request","text":"Land the brokered-market design note and the use-cases regrouping: head e3725505c798fab88165e1a8b87447cd422feeea on branch planner/market-and-use-cases-20261020 (pushed), three paths.\n\nWhat the head holds:\n- notes/2026-10-20-market-application-design.md (new, draft 1): a brokered market as a dap application. A roster room where each provider enrolls their own offer (the consent record), one engagement room per need, and a site that reads them. Members, grants and acts in section 3; why the buyer stays outside in section 4; why two scopes serve instead of private views in section 5; the personal agents' part and the connector routes in section 6; what exists and what is missing in section 7; slices M1 to M4 in section 8; open questions in section 9; sources. It commissions nothing.\n- docs/use-cases.md: cases 46 (grow operation, Built), 47 (learning project), 48 to 50 (prospect room, bid response, marketing calendar) and 51 (brokered market) added from the notes they cite; the former group 3 \"Private views\" split by one test, whether one party holds the shared decision for the others: cases 21, 32, 37, 39, 40 and 41 move to a new group 3 \"Separate scopes, one authority\" (needs messages between an application's own scopes); group 4 \"Private views in one record\" keeps 42 and the sweep's club and kanban board; groups 5 and 6 renumbered; the \"Also needs\" lines of 08, 18, 19, 24, 25 and 33 now point at group 3's shape; header counts and the Source paragraph updated.\n- docs/roadmap.md: the two capability rows' use-case lists, the private-views section (a new paragraph \"What separate scopes cover\"), the messages-between-scopes section (the market would be the first declared application with scopes of its own), and the group anchors and numbers.\n\nDirection from Hugh, 20 October 2026: fold the private-views split into the use-cases doc, since it changes the breakdown by requirement; bring the doc up to date with the grow room, the market and the other designs since it was written; draft the market design note; hand over to the planner for landing.\n\nChecks run at the head: git diff --check against origin/main clean; every relative link and anchor in the three files resolves (scripted check); the hosted grow page answered 200. The gate's typecheck and tests do not read these files.\n\nNext for the planner: review-request to the checker at this head; answer findings with a new revision on the same branch; ratify and land on main as a planner head (gs merge --as planner from the clean shared checkout after fast-forward). A follow-up head may fix the path typo list the checker finds; no implementation request follows from this note until Hugh orders it.","body":{"conditions":"Checker review at the exact head before landing; findings answered by a new revision on the same branch; lands on main as a planner head; no implementation request follows from the note until Hugh orders it.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}